WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.870
Nostalgia is a powerful force, able to warp
people's perceptions.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.550
But you know what they say: you can't go home
again, something that anybody who's tried

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.880
to watch their favorite childhood shows as
an adult can confirm.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.800
Sometimes it's best to just leave well enough
alone and not revisit the past, as proven

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.400
by these TV shows that have become unwatchable
with age.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.759
Full House

00:00:20.759 --> 00:00:25.050
If you were like most kids in the late '80s,
you were probably parked in front of ABC's

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.710
family-friendly TGIF block every Friday night.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:32.500
And your parents probably hated every second
of it, because Full House's saccharine morality

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.829
and terrible puns were just flat out hard
to stomach.

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:38.670
“Remember that sausage and lima bean casserole
I made?

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.469
I called it my ‘Sunday Surprise.’”

00:00:40.469 --> 00:00:42.509
“We called it our ‘Monday Surprise.’”

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.780
“I was still getting surprised on Tuesday.”

00:00:46.789 --> 00:00:49.360
A hundred terrible catchphrases later...

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.710
"You got it dude."

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:55.760
...we're reminded just how awkward and unfunny
the original show was, especially now that

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.640
the series' continuation, Fuller House, has
gotten past the first season on Netflix.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:01.920
"Have mercy."

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.199
Xena: Warrior Princess

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.560
Xena: Warrior Princess is mainly remembered
for the way it challenged female stereotypes

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:12.330
and the discussions that raged over its lesbian
subtext.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:16.700
And it also gave the world Lucy Lawless, for
which we offer our heartfelt thanks.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.590
However, the importance of the show has kind
of papered over the fact that it's...not actually

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:25.360
very good, with iffy production values and
clumsy directing.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:30.950
Not to mention random tonal shifts, like hyper
violence suddenly giving way to musical numbers.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.970
We'll always love Xena the cultural phenomenon.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:34.930
But the show itself?

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:36.160
Not so much.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.200
Highlander: The Series

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.980
Twenty years ago, Highlander: The Series was
about as good as it got for high fantasy.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:43.980
Now?

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.700
We have Game of Thrones.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.700
And once you've seen that, or any other modern
television epic, it's hard to go back to Highlander's

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.960
outdated special effects, repetitive immortal-of-the-month
scripts, and one-note acting.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.770
The show kept telling us there could only
be one.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:01.270
Well… this ain't it.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:02.500
Saved by the Bell

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.450
While '90s spinoffs Saved by the Bell: The
College Years and Saved by the Bell: The New

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:11.820
Class have always been pretty unwatchable,
the original show was once considered essential

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:12.820
television.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:16.860
Digging out the NBC high school sitcom for
your kids to watch today isn't advisable,

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.520
however, as many of the lessons are painfully
dated.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.730
“Haven’t you ever heard of the women’s
movement?”

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:22.730
“Well sure.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.840
Put on something cute and move it into the
kitchen.”

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.630
If you want your kids to experience cool high
school entertainment, just buy them some Archie

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:32.840
comics and spare them this horribly out of
touch television.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:34.450
Walker, Texas Ranger

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:39.450
The fact that Chuck Norris has become a living
parody of this character is almost — but

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:44.790
not quite — enough to prepare you for a
return visit to the unapologetically manly

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:45.990
Walker, Texas Ranger.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:50.340
While Norris is clearly a skilled martial
artist, he struggles with pretty much everything

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.720
else asked of him here.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.090
And he's not the only one.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:55.380
“And how you doin’ little pardner?”

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.940
“Fine, and it’s little visitor now.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.959
Adadamdvhidohi is how you say it in Cherokee.”

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:05.710
“Oooh, well pardon my French, but uh...I’ll
be damned.”

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.860
“Walker told me I have AIDS.”

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:12.610
How bad is Walker, Texas Ranger?

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:16.890
One of Conan O'Brien's most beloved comedy
routines is simply playing clips from the

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:17.890
show.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:18.890
That about says it all.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:22.640
“My Walker, Texas Ranger lever right here.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.069
Let’s give it a shot and see how it works.”

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:28.540
“Amigo!”

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:32.950
Baywatch

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:38.400
At its height, Baywatch was one of America's
most highly coveted exports, commanding over

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.660
a billion weekly viewers from more than 148
countries.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:46.310
But looking back at the show today it's plain
to see that the skin routinely on display

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:48.460
was literally the only appeal.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:52.850
With nowhere near enough drama to warrant
an hour-long slot, Baywatch fills the gaps

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:57.540
with copious amounts of running, normally
presented in slow motion to not only capture

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:01.612
the females’ bouncing chests in all their
glory, but to make up for the fact that there

00:04:01.612 --> 00:04:03.540
isn't much else going on.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.430
Critics at the time hated it.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:09.220
It may have taken nearly two decades, but
fans are finally catching up.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:10.569
Thanks for watching!

